# Night / week-ahead images — Sacred Ground in the picture

Campaign `week_ahead` (daily ~7:00 PM America/Chicago) night plates live in
`config/image_atmosphere.json` → `nighttime.creative_pool` (+ holidays / full moon /
season storefronts).

## Hard rule (Founder — Aug 6, 2026)

**Every night creative must include a clear Sacred Ground visual anchor baked into
the photograph itself** — not only Autopilot’s logo corner + text overlays.

Acceptable in-photo anchors (any one is enough if obvious at a glance):

- Lit **Sacred Ground storefront** (eggplant awnings / neon / window glow with name)
- Circular **logo / folk-art sun face** as a **small** sky mark, moon inset, or bat-signal
  (not a daytime sun dominating the frame)
- **“Sacred Ground” / “SACRED GROUND”** glowing in sky, clouds, mountains, or neon
- Searchlights / light beams projecting the name or circular logo (“bat signal”)

## Hard rule (Founder — Aug 10, 2026) — real storefront resemblance

Creative surroundings are OK (mountains, side streets, water, celestial skies).

**When a shop / building facade appears in frame**, it must resemble the **real
Sacred Ground storefront** customers would recognize:

- Front of shop, **eggplant-purple awning**, tan stone architecture
- White **SACRED GROUND** lettering on the awning (blank space between words — no swoosh)
- Reference look: `assets/sg-night-fall.png`, `assets/sg-night-summer.png`,
  `assets/sg-example-night-fall-storefront.png`, `assets/refs/exterior-*.png`

**Banned:** invented / fantasy shop facades (Victorian fairy-tale fronts, corrugated
metal rooftops, generic neon-only silhouettes, random apothecary buildings that are
not Sacred Ground’s awning + architecture).

Also restore the **circular sun logo** bottom-left of the photo area
(`config/brand/sacred-ground-logo-circle-transparent.png`, ~10–13% width, 80–90%
opacity) on social plates — bake into prebranded plates when overlays do not run.

## Hard rule (Founder — Aug 9, 2026) — night mood + no-repeat

- Night posts must look like **night** (night sky / lit storefront / neon / aurora) —
  **not daytime sun**.
- Retire sun-dominating plates (`daytime_sun: true`, family `daytime_sun`) under
  `creative_pool_retired_daytime_sun` — never pick them for `week_ahead`.
- Do **not** reuse the same night URL two nights in a row; prefer
  `nighttime.no_repeat_days` cooldown (default 7).

## Not enough

- Pure generic northern lights, Milky Way, star trails, moonlit lake, meadow, temple,
  or sacred-geometry sky **with no SG name, logo-sun, or storefront**
- Relying only on the Autopilot overlay logo + “NEXT …” text + cream footer
  (those still apply for non-prebranded posts — see `social-image-branding.mdc` —
  but they do **not** replace an in-photo SG anchor)
- Large daytime sun / sunrise / sun-in-sky plates (even with the SG folk-art face)

## Pool hygiene

- Active `creative_pool` entries should be `sg_identity: "pass"` only and **not**
  `daytime_sun`
- Failures / pending regens live under `creative_pool_needs_sg_identity` until replaced
- Sun-dominant retires live under `creative_pool_retired_daytime_sun`
- Prefer regenerating worst offenders first (pure aurora / sky with zero SG cue)
- New plates: save under `assets/sg-night-creative-*.png`, upload via WP `upload_media`,
  wire URL into atmosphere; keep local PNG as source of truth

## Do not

- Do not republish an already-live tonight post just to swap the creative
- Do not treat overlay branding as satisfying this rule
- Do not put event lists or prices on the night photo (events stay in caption)
